  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It builds the bar ring with Aura3D and passes the typecheck. I had no browser or shell here, so I did not run `vite build` and have not seen a rendered frame.\n\n- **Bars:** 64 boxes sit in a circle of radius 4 on a grey floor plane. They are one `instances.box` node, so they draw as a single instanced call. Each bar faces the ring centre.\n- **Animation:** every frame, each bar's height comes from a mix of three sine waves, which `app.onFrame` writes back through `setInstances`.\n- **Colour:** each bar has its own `hsl()` colour, with the hue stepping evenly around the ring. The material is white, so the colours aren't applied twice.\n- **Lighting:** a neutral environment, a hemisphere light, a blue fill light, and a directional key light with soft PCF shadows that fall on the floor.\n- **Camera:** `camera.orbit` with `autoRotate: 0.2` circles the ring slowly.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frame callback, and again after `app.ready()`. The engine owns the render loop, so I didn't add a separate `requestAnimationFrame` loop.\n\nI haven't judged the shadow framing, the bar heights against the camera distance, or the colours. They may need a tweak once you see a frame.\n\n",
